# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Lixus AI - Environment variables
# Copy this file to `.env` and adjust values for your environment.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Database -------------------------------------------------------------------
# PostgreSQL connection string. On Railway, add a PostgreSQL database and
# reference its variable (e.g. ${{ Postgres.DATABASE_URL }}).
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/lixus?schema=public"

# Auth -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Used to sign session JWTs. Generate a strong value, e.g.:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
AUTH_SECRET="dev-secret-change-me-please-32-bytes-min"

# Canonical public base URL. Used for anything that leaves our trust boundary
# (email verify links, OAuth redirect_uri) — NEVER the request Host header, which
# is client-controllable (host-header injection). Set to your real domain in prod.
APP_URL="https://www.lixusai.com"

# ── DEPLOYMENT LOCALE / CURRENCY ────────────────────────────────────────────
# All OPTIONAL. Unset = the shipped .com behaviour (tr-TR, TRY, current prices);
# leaving this whole block out changes nothing.
#
# .com and .eu are SEPARATE deployments with their own env and database, which is
# why this lives here and not in a database column: one database never mixes
# customers who should be billed in different currencies.
#
# NOTHING here converts money. Setting a currency only changes the LABEL, so a
# deployment that bills in another currency MUST also set that currency's prices —
# otherwise the lira amounts would be shown with a foreign symbol.
#
# THIS IS A HARD BOOT GATE, NOT A WARNING. If APP_BILLING_CURRENCY is anything
# other than TRY, then ALL SIX of these are REQUIRED and production refuses to
# start (exit 1) if ANY of them is missing:
#     PLAN_PRICE_BASLANGIC_MINOR   PADDLE_PRICE_BASLANGIC
#     PLAN_PRICE_PRO_MINOR         PADDLE_PRICE_PRO
#     PLAN_PRICE_ISLETME_MINOR     PADDLE_PRICE_ISLETME
# The PLAN_PRICE_* values are what we DISPLAY; the PADDLE_PRICE_* ids decide what
# is actually CHARGED. Configuring one set without the other is how a customer
# ends up seeing one currency and being billed in another. A PARTIAL set is
# rejected too — the plans left unset are exactly the ones that would lie, and a
# half-filled config is the one most likely to look finished.
#
# Nothing here converts anything, and the code enforces the same pairing at
# runtime: if the prices for a non-TRY currency are incomplete, BOTH the currency
# and the partial prices are ignored and the shipped TRY pair is used, so no
# amount is ever printed with a currency it isn't denominated in.
#
# What this canNOT check: a Paddle price id is an opaque `pri_...` string, so its
# DENOMINATION is unverifiable from env. Confirm that by hand against the Paddle
# account when bringing a non-TRY deployment up.
#
# Reservation amounts (guest bookings) and Invoice rows (real Paddle charges) are
# NOT affected: each carries its own currency from its own source, and that always
# wins over anything set here. Organization.timezone never implies a currency.
#
# APP_LOCALE — number/date formatting only. Must be a locale this runtime has
# DATA for; "zz-ZZ" is well-formed BCP-47 but has none and is rejected at boot
# (it would silently format as the default instead of what you asked for).
# APP_LOCALE="tr-TR"
#
# APP_BILLING_CURRENCY — what WE charge for a subscription. CLOSED LIST: only
# "TRY" or "EUR" are accepted, and anything else stops the boot. Not a format
# check — Intl will happily render "EUU 1.00" or "ZZZ 1.00", so a single mistyped
# letter used to reach production. Supporting another currency needs three plan
# prices and three Paddle price ids denominated in it, so it is a code change.
# (This governs the SUBSCRIPTION only; a guest booking in USD is unaffected.)
# APP_BILLING_CURRENCY="TRY"
#
# APP_DEFAULT_TIMEZONE — IANA zone for NEW organizations on this deployment.
# Unset = Europe/Istanbul (the shipped .com answer and the existing column
# default, so leaving it out changes nothing for anyone). The host can change it
# any time in Ayarlar. With APP_TRUST_BROWSER_TIMEZONE off (the default) this is
# simply THE zone every new org gets.
# NOT inferred from APP_LOCALE or APP_BILLING_CURRENCY — a Berlin host can be
# billed in TRY, and a de-DE interface says nothing about where anyone sits.
# Must be a zone Intl accepts; a typo stops the boot rather than silently
# putting every new org on the Istanbul calendar.
# APP_DEFAULT_TIMEZONE="Europe/Istanbul"
#
# APP_TRUST_BROWSER_TIMEZONE — set to 1 (or true) to let the sign-up form's
# reported zone win over APP_DEFAULT_TIMEZONE. DEFAULT OFF, and off is right for
# .com: every customer is a Turkish host with Turkish properties, so the browser
# can only introduce a wrong answer (someone signing up while travelling) with
# nothing to gain — and a wrong zone is near-invisible, showing up as automated
# messages at odd hours rather than as an obvious fault. Turn it on for a
# genuinely multi-timezone deployment (.eu). The client reports its zone either
# way; this decides whether the server believes it. Anything but 1/true reads as
# off, so a typo costs a deterministic default rather than a wrong one.
# APP_TRUST_BROWSER_TIMEZONE=""
#
# Plan prices in MINOR UNITS (kuruş/cent) — whole integers, never decimals.
# Defaults: 44900 / 89900 / 169900 (₺449 / ₺899 / ₺1.699).
# PLAN_PRICE_BASLANGIC_MINOR="44900"
# PLAN_PRICE_PRO_MINOR="89900"
# PLAN_PRICE_ISLETME_MINOR="169900"

# ENCRYPTION_KEY — encrypts secrets at rest (e.g. each customer's own
# Hospitable token). REQUIRED in production: the boot gate (prestart) refuses
# to start when it is missing, a placeholder, or EQUAL to AUTH_SECRET — it must
# be its own independent value. Keep it STABLE forever: changing it makes every
# stored token unreadable (customers must re-connect). The AUTH_SECRET fallback
# in crypto.ts is a DEV-ONLY convenience, never a production instruction.
#   openssl rand -base64 32
ENCRYPTION_KEY=""

# QR_PIN_PEPPER — server pepper for the per-reservation QR chat PIN HMAC (Faz 5).
# REQUIRED IN PRODUCTION when QR_PIN_ENABLED=1: the boot gate (prestart) refuses
# to start if it is missing, a placeholder, shorter than 32 chars, or EQUAL to
# AUTH_SECRET — so the PIN hash never falls back to the session secret. With the
# feature OFF it is not needed (deploy never blocked). NOTE: rotating it
# invalidates every existing PIN (hosts simply regenerate) — the PIN is a
# short-lived per-stay code, so that's acceptable (unlike ENCRYPTION_KEY).
#   openssl rand -base64 32
QR_PIN_PEPPER=""

# SUPERADMIN_EMAILS — comma-separated operator emails who can access the Operator
# Panel (/admin): create customer orgs and enter (impersonate) them. Default EMPTY
# = nobody is a super-admin (panel inaccessible). Set this to YOUR login email.
SUPERADMIN_EMAILS=""

# AI Layer (optional) --------------------------------------------------------
# If OPENAI_API_KEY is empty, the app uses a deterministic template-based
# fallback so reply suggestions still work without any external API.
# OPENAI_MODEL = main guest replies (production: gpt-5.1).
# OPENAI_TRANSLATE_MODEL / OPENAI_STYLE_MODEL = optional overrides (fall back to OPENAI_MODEL).
OPENAI_API_KEY=""
OPENAI_MODEL="gpt-5.1"
OPENAI_TRANSLATE_MODEL=""
OPENAI_STYLE_MODEL=""

# Prep-plan AI summary (OPTIONAL, cosmetic) ----------------------------------
# Powers the "AI özeti oluştur" button on /hazirlik — a short natural-language
# gloss of the deterministic shopping/prep list. Any OpenAI-COMPATIBLE endpoint
# works (e.g. akashML). Unset SUPPLY_AI_API_KEY → the button is hidden and the
# deterministic list stands alone. Only aggregate numbers are sent, never guest PII.
SUPPLY_AI_API_KEY=""
SUPPLY_AI_BASE_URL="https://api.akashml.com/v1"
# akashML's GLM-5.2 slug. If the provider changes the id, set it here.
SUPPLY_AI_MODEL="zai-org/GLM-5.2"
# ⚠️ COUPLING: the GLM shadow classifier below FALLS BACK to SUPPLY_AI_API_KEY /
# SUPPLY_AI_BASE_URL when its own SHADOW_AI_* values are unset. With
# SHADOW_AI_ENABLED=1, setting this "cosmetic" key therefore ALSO ships REDACTED
# guest message bodies to the same provider — not just aggregate numbers.

# GLM shadow classifier pilot (OPTIONAL, default OFF) ------------------------
# Phase-1 comparison-only second model: on every auto-reply gate decision the
# REDACTED guest message (name→[Misafir], phone/email/codes masked) is classified
# by GLM via an OpenAI-compatible endpoint and the verdict is stored NEXT TO the
# code gate's decision (ShadowVerdict). ZERO decision authority. Stops silently
# after SHADOW_AI_SAMPLE_CAP rows. /admin shows the agreement card.
SHADOW_AI_ENABLED=""
# RECOMMENDED for a single-org pilot: comma-separated org allowlist. EMPTY = the
# shadow runs for EVERY eligible org — i.e. every customer's redacted messages go
# to the third-party processor. Pin it to the pilot org id(s).
SHADOW_AI_ORG_IDS=""
# Unset → falls back to SUPPLY_AI_API_KEY / SUPPLY_AI_BASE_URL (same akashML acct).
SHADOW_AI_API_KEY=""
SHADOW_AI_BASE_URL=""
SHADOW_AI_MODEL="zai-org/GLM-5.2"
# Pilot ceiling — the shadow stops after this many stored verdicts (default 200).
SHADOW_AI_SAMPLE_CAP=""

# Claude quality auditor (OPTIONAL, operator-only) ---------------------------
# Powers the /admin "Kalite Denetimi" card: Claude READS a redacted sample of
# recent AI replies and reports quality findings (it can never send messages or
# change prompts). Unset → the card shows "not configured"; boot is unaffected.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=""
QUALITY_AUDIT_MODEL=""

# Email ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Production path is Resend (preferred). Set RESEND_API_KEY + a verified
# RESEND_FROM address. Alternatively use SMTP (EMAIL_* below). If neither is
# configured, emails are logged to the console (dev only).
RESEND_API_KEY=""
RESEND_FROM="Lixus AI <noreply@lixusai.com>"
EMAIL_FROM="Lixus AI <noreply@lixusai.com>"
EMAIL_HOST=""
EMAIL_PORT="587"
EMAIL_USER=""
EMAIL_PASS=""

# Hospitable Public API v2 (Airbnb / Booking.com messaging) -----------------
# Hospitable unifies your channels (Airbnb, Booking, direct) and exposes guest
# messaging via an API. We use it to pull guest messages into the inbox and send
# replies back to the guest on their original channel.
# Docs: https://developer.hospitable.com/docs/public-api-docs
#
# MULTI-TENANT: each organization now connects its OWN Hospitable account from
# Settings (token stored encrypted per-org). HOSPITABLE_API_TOKEN below is only a
# FALLBACK for the founder's original ("primary") org so the original setup keeps
# working; new customer orgs must connect their own. The primary org is ONLY
# the one named by PRIMARY_ORG_ID. In production there is NO fallback (unset ⇒
# the env token is used by nobody); the oldest-org fallback exists in dev/demo only.
#
# HOSPITABLE_API_TOKEN — Personal Access Token (Hospitable → Settings → API).
#                        Leave empty once every org has connected its own.
# HOSPITABLE_API_BASE_URL — optional override (defaults to production v2).
# PRIMARY_ORG_ID — optional: explicit org id allowed to use the env token above.
HOSPITABLE_API_TOKEN=""
HOSPITABLE_API_BASE_URL=""
PRIMARY_ORG_ID=""

# Hospitable OAuth vendor flow — one-click "Hospitable ile Bağlan" (Settings).
# DORMANT unless client id+secret are set: the manual Personal Access Token
# flow above keeps working unconditionally either way.
# HOSPITABLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID / _SECRET — REQUIRED. From the Hospitable Partner
#   Portal (partners.hospitable.com → Settings → API → Clients → New client).
# HOSPITABLE_OAUTH_AUTHORIZE_URL / _TOKEN_URL — optional overrides. Default to
#   Hospitable's documented OAuth2 endpoints (auth.hospitable.com/oauth/...);
#   only set these if Hospitable ever changes them.
# HOSPITABLE_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URI — optional override; must exactly match what's
#   registered on the client in the Partner Portal. Defaults to the production
#   callback URL below.
HOSPITABLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=""
HOSPITABLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=""
HOSPITABLE_OAUTH_AUTHORIZE_URL=""
HOSPITABLE_OAUTH_TOKEN_URL=""
HOSPITABLE_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URI=""

# Scheduled sync (production 24/7) -------------------------------------------
# Secret that protects the scheduled sync + night auto-reply endpoint
# (/api/cron/sync). Your hosting scheduler must send this value as either
# "Authorization: Bearer <secret>" or an "x-cron-secret" header. A ?secret=
# query param is deliberately NOT accepted (it would leak into request logs).
# Generate one with: openssl rand -base64 32
# Leave empty in local dev to keep the endpoint disabled (returns 401).
CRON_SECRET=""

# Alerts & monitoring --------------------------------------------------------
# Where complaint/refund alerts are emailed (needs SMTP configured above).
ALERT_EMAIL=""
# Where system error reports are emailed (falls back to ALERT_EMAIL if unset).
ERROR_ALERT_EMAIL=""
# Optional Sentry DSN. When set, system errors are also sent to Sentry
# (dependency-free, via the ingest envelope API). Leave empty to disable.
SENTRY_DSN=""

# Disable the in-process 2-minute scheduler if you rely only on external cron.
INTERNAL_CRON_DISABLED=""

# KVKK retention (months). Set (e.g. 24) to anonymize guest PII on stays older
# than N months during deep syncs. EMPTY = retention sweep OFF. Prod: 24.
DATA_RETENTION_MONTHS=""
# Marketing-lead retention (months). EMPTY = never purged.
LEAD_RETENTION_MONTHS=""
# Reverse-trial reminder e-mails ("ending soon"/"ended"). 1 = enabled (prod: 1).
TRIAL_EMAILS_ENABLED=""
TRIAL_REMINDER_DAYS=""
# Sync window tuning (days). Defaults: 90/120 frequent, 540/540 deep, deep hourly.
HOSPITABLE_SYNC_BACK_DAYS=""
HOSPITABLE_SYNC_FORWARD_DAYS=""
HOSPITABLE_DEEP_BACK_DAYS=""
HOSPITABLE_DEEP_FORWARD_DAYS=""
HOSPITABLE_DEEP_EVERY_MIN=""
# Base URL used in e-mail links (default https://www.lixusai.com).
APP_BASE_URL=""
# Hours the AI stays silent after a guest asks for a human (org setting wins).
HUMAN_HANDOFF_HOLD_HOURS=""
# Set 0 to globally strip the "(otomatik hazırlandı)" note from auto-replies.
AUTO_REPLY_DISCLOSURE=""
# Dunning grace days for past_due subscriptions (default 14).
BILLING_PAST_DUE_GRACE_DAYS=""
# Set 1 ONLY when the origin is locked behind Cloudflare: trusts the
# cf-connecting-ip header for rate limiting. Default off = rightmost XFF hop.
TRUST_CF_HEADER=""
# Set 1 to make x-real-ip authoritative for rate limiting (Railway documents it
# as the edge-set client IP). ONLY enable after checking a LIVE request's headers
# on the deployment: x-real-ip must be OVERWRITTEN by the platform (not passed
# through from the client), else callers could spoof their rate-limit identity.
# Default off = rightmost XFF hop (today's behaviour).
TRUST_X_REAL_IP=""

# Feature flags --------------------------------------------------------------
# REGISTRATION_OPEN=1 → public self-serve /register is enabled.
# AUTO_REPLY_ENABLED=1 → master switch for automatic guest replies.
# GUEST_CHAT_ENABLED=1 → global kill-switch for the QR guest concierge.
# LANDING_DEMO_ENABLED=1 → public "try the AI" demo on the landing page
#   (unauthenticated OpenAI spend → per-IP rate limit + LANDING_DEMO_DAILY_CAP
#   global daily ceiling, default 300). Off by default.
# QR_ESCALATION_EMAIL_ENABLED=1 → e-mail the host when the QR guest chat
#   escalates ("mesajınızı ilettim"). DEFAULT OFF. Minimal content (no guest
#   text), deduped per event, recipient = org alertEmail → oldest OWNER.
# QR_PIN_ENABLED=1 → per-reservation QR chat PIN (Faz 5). DEFAULT OFF. When on,
#   the host can generate a 6-digit PIN per reservation; the guest must enter it
#   to claim the chat on their device (closes the "wrong scanner claims the stay"
#   gap). Deploying with it OFF changes NOTHING for existing chats. Old reservations
#   (no PIN) keep the first-scan device-binding flow unless the org turns on strict
#   mode (Ayarlar → Misafir Chat → "Tüm konaklamalarda giriş kodu zorunlu").
# DURABLE_OUTBOX_ENABLED=1 → route outbound guest-channel sends through the durable
#   outbox (#8): the message + send-intent are written atomically and a worker
#   delivers with claim/retry/reconcile. DEFAULT OFF. When OFF the live send path is
#   EXACTLY the proven claim-then-send. Wired (flag ON): manual host reply, AI auto-reply,
#   holding-ack, welcome/check-in/check-out (migration 30). QR internal messages are
#   excluded. No exactly-once claim (Hospitable has no idempotency key) → ambiguous → review.
#   Enable only after verifying the worker drains in your env (see DEPLOYMENT.md §6).
# ICAL_DISAPPEARANCE_RECONCILE_ENABLED=1 → reflect an upstream cancellation when a booking
#   SILENTLY vanishes from an iCal feed (#23, FAZ 2). DEFAULT OFF. Heavily guarded: cancels a
#   FUTURE, source-bound stay ONLY after it is absent from >=2 consecutive RELIABLE feed runs
#   AND for >=24h; empty / suspicious-drop / failed fetches never count; reappearing resets it;
#   never DELETEs data (status flip + system-task cleanup only). iCal sync is user-triggered.
# STORAGE_ENABLED=1 → store NEW task photos in a PRIVATE S3/R2 bucket + serve them via
#   short-lived signed URLs, instead of the local public /uploads path. DEFAULT OFF. When OFF the
#   upload path is byte-identical to before; existing /uploads files are NEVER migrated or deleted.
#   Serving + the deletion queue work whenever the CREDENTIALS are set (independent of this flag),
#   so a flag-off rollback never breaks photos already in the bucket. See DEPLOYMENT.md §7.
REGISTRATION_OPEN=""
AUTO_REPLY_ENABLED=""
GUEST_CHAT_ENABLED=""
# EMAIL_OUTBOX_ENABLED=1 → identity e-mails (verify / password reset & change
# codes) are queued in the durable EmailOutbox and delivered by the in-process
# 15s poller + the 2-min cron (docs/EMAIL-OUTBOX-DESIGN.md). Removes the
# synchronous provider call from those requests (timing parity + outage
# resilience). Default OFF = today's synchronous sends. NOTE: with
# INTERNAL_CRON_DISABLED=1 the poller is off too — delivery latency becomes
# your external scheduler's interval (also schedule /api/cron/email-outbox
# externally for fast delivery in that setup).
EMAIL_OUTBOX_ENABLED=""
QR_ESCALATION_EMAIL_ENABLED=""
QR_PIN_ENABLED=""
DURABLE_OUTBOX_ENABLED=""
ICAL_DISAPPEARANCE_RECONCILE_ENABLED=""
STORAGE_ENABLED=""
LANDING_DEMO_ENABLED=""
LANDING_DEMO_DAILY_CAP=""

# Private object storage (S3-compatible) — REQUIRED only when STORAGE_ENABLED is on (prestart
# gate enforces; never prints a value). Endpoint MUST be https. Region defaults to "auto".
#
# STORAGE_BUCKET must be the name EXACTLY as the provider shows it — several append a unique
# suffix (e.g. "lixus-uploads-ssokr6h6veq"), and the display name in their UI is not always the
# real one. It is validated against the S3 charset at boot: lowercase only. Uppercase silently
# produced a null config before that check existed, so storage looked configured and wasn't.
#
# STORAGE_PATH_STYLE — address objects as {endpoint}/{bucket}/{key} instead of the default
# {bucket}.{endpointHost}/{key}. LEAVE EMPTY unless the provider requires path-style: Tigris
# (which backs Railway Buckets) dropped it for buckets created after Feb 2025, and AWS has
# deprecated it. Set to 1 only for something like a self-hosted MinIO. Getting this wrong does
# not look like an addressing problem — every call returns SignatureDoesNotMatch, because the
# host and path are both part of what gets signed.
STORAGE_ENDPOINT=""
STORAGE_BUCKET=""
STORAGE_REGION=""
STORAGE_ACCESS_KEY_ID=""
STORAGE_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=""
STORAGE_PATH_STYLE=""

# Billing / Payments (Faz 2 — DORMANT until configured) ----------------------
# Iyzico (Türkiye). Leave empty to keep ALL billing code dormant. Sandbox keys
# from the Iyzico merchant panel let us build & test before going live.
IYZICO_API_KEY=""
IYZICO_SECRET_KEY=""
# Defaults to the sandbox endpoint when empty. Live: https://api.iyzipay.com
IYZICO_BASE_URL=""
# Shared secret guarding /api/webhooks/iyzico. Empty = endpoint disabled
# (returns 200, stores nothing) so it can't be abused before launch.
IYZICO_WEBHOOK_SECRET=""
# Paddle Billing (Merchant of Record — used when the seller is the Italian
# Partita IVA entity; Paddle collects/remits VAT so no per-country tax reg).
# Leave empty to keep the Paddle code dormant. PADDLE_ENV: sandbox | production.
PADDLE_API_KEY=""
PADDLE_ENV=""
# Signing secret of the Paddle notification destination. Empty = /api/webhooks/
# paddle disabled (returns 200, stores nothing) until billing goes live.
PADDLE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=""
# Paddle PRICE ids (pri_...) for each tier — maps webhook items → plan code.
# REQUIRED (all three) on any deployment where APP_BILLING_CURRENCY is not TRY;
# the boot gate refuses to start without them. See the currency block near the top.
PADDLE_PRICE_BASLANGIC=""
PADDLE_PRICE_PRO=""
PADDLE_PRICE_ISLETME=""
# Paddle.js (client-side checkout overlay). Client token + env (sandbox|production).
NEXT_PUBLIC_PADDLE_CLIENT_TOKEN=""
NEXT_PUBLIC_PADDLE_ENV=""
# Master switch for paywall ENFORCEMENT. Empty/false = nothing is EVER blocked
# (existing customers safe). Set "true" ONLY after backfilling existing orgs as
# active. See ROADMAP.md Faz 2. When "true": expired reverse-trials + lapsed
# subscriptions see the upgrade screen instead of the app (operators bypass).
BILLING_ENFORCED=""
# Reverse-trial length in days (default 14). New signups get full Pro free for
# this long with no card; if not upgraded, access pauses ONLY when enforced.
TRIAL_DAYS=""
# In-app plan change (upgrade/downgrade via Paddle subscription PATCH). Default
# OFF: the billing page then only offers checkout/portal. Set "1" to enable the
# preview→confirm upgrade/downgrade flow (verified live on prod, 2026-07-13).
PADDLE_PLAN_CHANGE_ENABLED=""

# Landing page (optional) ----------------------------------------------------
# WhatsApp business number (digits only, e.g. 905xxxxxxxxx) → shows a WhatsApp
# button. Demo video must be an EMBED url (youtube.com/embed/.. or Loom embed).
NEXT_PUBLIC_WHATSAPP=""
NEXT_PUBLIC_DEMO_VIDEO=""

# App ------------------------------------------------------------------------
NODE_ENV="development"
